    <h2>1. What is CSS?</h2>
    <p><b>CSS</b> means <b>Cascading Style Sheets</b>. It is used to <b>design and style</b> a website - colors, fonts, size, spacing, layout, buttons, cards.</p>
    <p>Think like this:</p>
    <p><b>HTML = Body (Structure)</b> - Head, hands, legs.<br><b>CSS = Clothes + Makeup (Design)</b> - Shirt color, style, beauty.</p>
    <div class="note"><b>Example:</b> Without CSS, a website looks like a plain newspaper. With CSS, it looks like Facebook, YouTube, Daraz - beautiful and colourful.</div>
    <h2>2. Without CSS vs With CSS</h2>
    <div class="result"><b>Without CSS (Only HTML):</b><p style="margin:8px 0">My Name is Ali</p><p style="margin:0">I am learning HTML.</p><p style="margin:8px 0 0">Button: [ Submit ] - Plain, no colour</p></div>
    <div class="result" style="margin-top:12px"><b>With CSS (HTML + CSS):</b><div class="demo-box">My Name is Ali</div><p style="text-align:center;color:#64748b">I am learning HTML.</p><div style="text-align:center"><button class="btn">Submit</button></div></div>
    <h2>3. CSS Syntax - Very Easy</h2>
    <p>CSS has 3 parts: <b>Selector + Property + Value</b></p>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">h1</span> <span class="text">{</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">color</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">red</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">font-size</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">30px</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span>
    </code></div>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Part</th><th>Meaning</th><th>In Example</th></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Selector</b></td><td>Which tag to style?</td><td>h1</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Property</b></td><td>What to change?</td><td>color, font-size</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>Value</b></td><td>What value to set?</td><td>red, 30px</td></tr>
    </table>
    <div class="note"><b>Rules:</b> Property and Value are separated by <b>:</b> colon. Every line ends with <b>;</b> semicolon. Full rule is inside <b>{ }</b> curly brackets.</div>
    <h2>4. 3 Ways to Add CSS</h2>
    <h3 style="margin-top:15px">Way 1: Inline CSS - Inside the Tag</h3>
    <p>Use <b>style=" "</b> attribute inside the tag. Best for one small change.</p>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;h1</span> <span class="attr">style</span>=<span class="val">"color:red;"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text">Hello</span><span class="tag">&lt;/h1&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="result"><b>Result:</b> <span class="demo-red">Hello</span></div>
    <h3 style="margin-top:15px">Way 2: Internal CSS - Inside &lt;style&gt; in &lt;head&gt;</h3>
    <p>Write all CSS in one place in head. Best for one page.</p>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;head&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;style&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">h1</span> <span class="text">{</span> <span class="attr">color</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">blue</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="text">}</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">p</span> <span class="text">{</span> <span class="attr">color</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">green</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="text">}</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;/style&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/head&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="result"><b>Result:</b> <span class="demo-blue">This heading is Blue</span><br><span style="color:#16a34a;font-weight:bold">This paragraph is Green</span></div>
    <h3 style="margin-top:15px">Way 3: External CSS - Separate File (Best Way)</h3>
    <p>Create a separate file <b>style.css</b> and link it. Best for real projects with many pages.</p>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">&lt;!-- In HTML head --&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;link</span> <span class="attr">rel</span>=<span class="val">"stylesheet"</span> <span class="attr">href</span>=<span class="val">"style.css"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">/* In style.css file */</span><br>
<span class="tag">h1</span> <span class="text">{</span> <span class="attr">color</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">red</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="text">}</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="note"><b>Which to use?</b> For learning - Internal CSS. For real projects - External CSS. For one small fix - Inline CSS.</div>
    <h2>5. Selectors - Tag, Class, ID</h2>
    <p>You learned class and id in Lesson 8. Now we use them in CSS:</p>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Selector</th><th>CSS Code</th><th>Styles</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Tag Selector</td><td>h1 { color:red; }</td><td>All h1 tags</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Class Selector ( . )</td><td>.card { color:blue; }</td><td>All elements with class="card"</td></tr>
      <tr><td>ID Selector ( # )</td><td>#header { color:green; }</td><td>Only element with id="header"</td></tr>
    </table>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">/* Tag Selector */</span><br>
<span class="tag">h1</span> <span class="text">{</span> <span class="attr">color</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">red</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="text">}</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">/* Class Selector - dot */</span><br>
<span class="tag">.card</span> <span class="text">{</span> <span class="attr">background</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">lightblue</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="text">}</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">/* ID Selector - hash */</span><br>
<span class="tag">#header</span> <span class="text">{</span> <span class="attr">background</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">black</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="text">}</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>6. Full Example - Style Your Lesson 10 Project</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">&lt;style&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">h1</span> <span class="text">{</span> <span class="attr">color</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">blue</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="attr">text-align</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">center</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="text">}</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">p</span> <span class="text">{</span> <span class="attr">color</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">grey</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="attr">font-size</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">18px</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="text">}</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">.card</span> <span class="text">{</span> <span class="attr">background</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">lightblue</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="attr">padding</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">20px</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="text">}</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/style&gt;</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="result"><b>Result:</b><h2 style="color:#2563eb;text-align:center;margin:0">Ali Khan</h2><p style="color:#64748b;font-size:18px;text-align:center;margin:5px 0">I am learning Web Development</p><div style="background:#e0f2fe;padding:20px;border-radius:10px;text-align:center">This is my Card - with .card CSS</div></div>
    <h2>7. Homework - Practice for 2 Minutes</h2>
    <p>In Playground, make this:</p>
    <p>1. One <b>h1</b> in red color<br>2. One <b>p</b> in blue color, font-size 20px<br>3. One <b>div class="card"</b> with background lightblue and padding 20px</p>
    <div class="box"><b>Remember:</b> CSS = Cascading Style Sheets | HTML = Structure, CSS = Design | Syntax = Selector { Property: Value; } | 3 Ways = Inline (style=" "), Internal (&lt;style&gt; in head), External (style.css + &lt;link&gt;) | Tag Selector = h1 | Class Selector = .card | ID Selector = #header</div>
    <p><b>Next Step:</b> After this lesson, go to <a href="/lesson12">Lesson 12 - Colors & Background</a> to learn colors, background-color, and gradients.</p>
    <a id="playgroundLink" class="btn" href="/playground">▶ Try it Yourself - Playground</a><br><br>
